# ==================================================================================#
# GWIscan architecture table — ARCHITECTURE mode (domain combinations)              #
# ==================================================================================#
# Copy this file to  config/architecture.tsv  and edit it for your study, and set
#   MODE: architecture   in config.yaml.
#
# Architecture mode identifies proteins that carry a COMBINATION of Pfam domains on
# one chain: a PRIMARY domain that defines and seeds the family, plus one or more
# REQUIRED domains that must also be present. Both are Pfam HMMs found by hmmscan.
#
# The search is two hmmscan passes, so a common domain (e.g. a kinase) is never
# scanned genome-wide:
#   1. hmmscan the whole proteome against the PRIMARY HMM(s)  -> candidate proteins.
#   2. hmmscan only those candidates against the primary+required HMMs, keeping the
#      ones that also carry every required domain. Those are the final candidates.
#
# The final candidates then go through the ordinary annotation pipeline unchanged:
# InterProScan does the complete domain/GO annotation, then ProtParam, TargetP,
# DeepLoc, genomic coordinates, and the compiled TSV/XLSX. `family` is the
# Architecture name, so every output groups by it.
#
# One row per architecture (family). TAB-separated. Whole-line '#' comments and
# blank lines are ignored.
#
# COLUMNS
#   Architecture  Family name. Used verbatim in the outputs. Required and unique.
#
#   Primary       The defining Pfam domain that seeds the genome-wide search. One
#                 slot; give alternatives with '|' (any one seeds). Choose the
#                 domain that best defines the family (often the rarer/ectodomain,
#                 so the candidate set stays small). Pfam accession(s) only.
#
#   Required      The Pfam domain(s) that must ALSO be present, '+'-separated (AND).
#                 Each slot may list '|' alternatives (OR), so a domain that two
#                 models describe is accepted from either, e.g. PF00069|PF07714
#                 accepts Pkinase OR Pkinase_Tyr. Pfam accession(s) only.
#
#   Class         Optional rollup label grouping architectures. Defaults to the
#                 Architecture name if blank ('-').
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three classic LecRLK subtypes, seeded on the lectin ectodomain (Pfams from
# the oat LecRLK study): G-type B_lectin PF01453, L-type Lectin_legB PF00139,
# C-type Lectin_C PF00059; the required kinase is Pkinase PF00069 or Pkinase_Tyr
# PF07714. Seed on the kinase instead (Primary PF00069, Required the lectin) if you
# want the more sensitive net at the cost of more candidates.
Architecture	Primary	Required	Class
G-LecRLK	PF01453	PF00069|PF07714	LecRLK
L-LecRLK	PF00139	PF00069|PF07714	LecRLK
C-LecRLK	PF00059	PF00069|PF07714	LecRLK
